1d:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"On the remote side"}],", the worker image is built with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"nix2container"}]," and\nits environment is composed entirely of ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/nix/store/…"}]," paths. The image is a\ncarrier for that closure rather than a conventional root filesystem."]}]
1e:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"On the local side"}],", entering the Nix development shell realizes the same\nderivations into your own ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/nix/store"}],". This is what the commented-out ",["$","code",null,{"children":"PATH"}],"\nlines in the generated ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre.bazelrc"}]," are for: Bazel ignores them, but Nix\nneeds a reason to fetch the closure, and those lines are it. The"]}]
