20:["$","p",null,{"children":["says so directly: \"all paths printed in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre.bazelrc"}]," will be available on\nyour local system.\""]}]
21:["$","p",null,{"children":["What is shared between local and remote is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"the store paths"}],", not the\nimage. Understanding that explains almost every question people have about\nLRE's edges."]}]
22:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-guarantee-with-its-qualifiers-intact","children":"The guarantee, with its qualifiers intact"}]
23:["$","p",null,{"children":"The source states the promise carefully, and the qualifiers are load-bearing:"}]
24:["$","blockquote",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["a framework to build, distribute, and rapidly iterate on custom toolchain\nsetups that are transparent, fully hermetic, and reproducible ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"across\nmachines of the same system architecture"}]," […] This lets you reuse build\nartifacts with ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"virtually"}]," perfect cache hit rate."]}],"\n"]}]
25:["$","p",null,{"children":["Both emphases are the source's meaning, not an editorial softening.\nReproducibility is claimed within an architecture, not across them; an\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"aarch64-darwin"}]," laptop and an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64-linux"}]," worker are not going to share\nC++ artifacts, because they are not running the same binaries. And \"virtually\nperfect\" acknowledges that the toolchain is one input among several, and LRE\nonly pins the toolchain."]}]
26:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":"$f:props:children:2:props:children:7:props:children:0:props:children"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"LRE is explicitly experimental"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The repository's own documentation opens with a warning that LRE is \"highly\nexperimental and can be challenging to set up in downstream projects\", and\na note that at the time of writing it \"only works on ",["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64-linux"}],"\". The\nRust toolchains have since grown to four systems; the C++ toolchain has\nnot. Treat the setup cost as real."]}]]}]]}]
27:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-is-pinned-and-what-is-not","children":"What is pinned, and what is not"}]
28:["$","p",null,{"children":"This is where careful reading pays off."}]
29:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not the image digest."}]," Every ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," value in the generated\nplatforms is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"name:tag"}],", where the tag is a Nix derivation hash, never a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"sha256:"}]," content digest. The upstream config generator's digest-resolution\nstep was deliberately patched out, with the in-source justification that\n\"skipping this hash is not a generally safe practice and only works for us\nbecause our images are reproducible.\""]}]
2a:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not a URL that gets pulled."}]," ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," is a ",["$","em",null,{"children":"raw string matched by\nthe scheduler"}]," against what a worker advertises. Forge does not fetch it.\nTwo different conventions coexist in-tree (",["$","code",null,{"children":"docker://lre-cc:<tag>"}]," for C++\nand a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ghcr.io/..."}]," reference for Rust), and a downstream user has to match\nwhatever string their own workers advertise. See\n",["$","$L3e",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"platform properties"}],"."]}]
2b:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not the image you actually deploy."}]," Three distinct images are in play: a\ngenerator image, the image the platform config nominally names, and the\nworker image that actually runs. The repository warns about this in its own\ndeployment manifests. The relationship is maintained by convention and by\ntag propagation, not by any mechanism that would catch a mismatch."]}]
2c:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Not a single shared closure."}]," The local closure is whatever the dev shell\nrealizes; the worker image's closure is that plus extras the worker needs.\nThey are compatible by construction, not identical."]}]
2d:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"coverage","children":"Coverage"}]
2e:["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Language"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Status"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Rust"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Full toolchains across four Nix systems, stable and nightly"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"C/C++"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Full toolchain, ",["$","strong",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64-linux"}]," only"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Java"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"An image and a generated runtime exist, but no Bazel toolchain is registered"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","strong",null,{"children":"Python, Go"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Not provided"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
2f:["$","p",null,{"children":["Windows is not supported. On macOS the C++ path has no local toolchain at\nall (the flake module only emits the C++ platform and toolchain flags on\nLinux), so an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre-cc"}]," action can only run on a Linux worker carrying the\nimage; you get hermeticity there, not locality."]}]
30:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-brand/40 bg-brand-soft/40 text-foreground","role":"note","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M12 16v-4M12 8h.01M12 22c5.523 0 10-4.477 10-10S17.523 2 12 2 2 6.477 2 12s4.477 10 10 10Z"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"LRE is not an offline mode"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"It is tempting to read \"local remote execution\" as \"remote execution without\nthe network\". It is not. LRE pins the toolchain; whether a given action\nruns locally or on a remote worker is a separate question decided by\nplatform matching. On the platforms where the toolchain exists locally,\nbuilds are local, but that is a consequence, not the guarantee."}]]}]]}]
31:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"why-nix-specifically","children":"Why Nix, specifically"}]
32:["$","p",null,{"children":"Because the design needs every tool the build invokes to be identified by a\nhash of everything that produced it, and to live at a path that encodes that\nhash. That is precisely what a Nix store path is."}]
33:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"/usr/bin/clang"}]," cannot be pinned. Its identity is whatever your package\nmanager last installed, it differs across machines that both call themselves\n\"Ubuntu 22.04\", and no amount of hashing the binary recovers the headers and\nlibraries it will reach for. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/nix/store/<hash>-clang-…"}]," has already answered\nall of those questions by existing."]}]
34:["$","p",null,{"children":["Everything else about LRE follows from that one property. The container\nimages, the generated Bazel toolchains, the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre.bazelrc"}],", all of it is\nplumbing to get those store paths onto both sides of the build."]}]
35:["$","p",null,{"children":["For Nix itself, see ",["$","$L3e",null,{"href":"/contribute/nix","children":"Develop with Nix"}],"."]}]
36:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"when-it-is-worth-it","children":"When it is worth it"}]
37:["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Situation"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"LRE?"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Cache hits are poor between developers and CI on the same architecture"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Yes; this is the case it was built for"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"You already build with Bazel and already use Nix"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Yes; the marginal cost is small"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["You want C++ hermeticity on ",["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64-linux"}]]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Yes"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Your fleet is mixed-architecture and you expected cross-arch sharing"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No; the guarantee does not extend there"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"You need Python or Go toolchains pinned"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Not yet"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"You are looking for sandboxing or isolation"}],["$","td",null,{"children":["No; different problem, see ",["$","$L3e",null,{"href":"/explanations/correctness-hermeticity","children":"correctness and hermeticity"}]]}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"You want a quick win with a low setup cost"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No; the source calls the setup challenging, and means it"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
