39:["$","p",null,{"children":["The flake-side and Bazel-side wiring, the regeneration commands, and the\ndownstream-project setup are in\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/tree/v1.6.5/local-remote-execution","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"local-remote-execution","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"local-remote-execution at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"local-remote-execution/"]}],".\nFor actually running it (the commands, and what is local versus remote once\nyou leave ",["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64-linux"}],") see\n",["$","$L3e",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/toolchains-and-hermeticity","children":"toolchains and hermeticity"}],",\nwhich is in the Remote execution section."]}]
3a:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"common-questions","children":"Common questions"}]
3b:["$","$L3f",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L40",null,{"title":"Does LRE replace a remote worker fleet?","id":"lre-vs-fleet","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"No, and it does not try to. LRE is about toolchain identity, not about\nwhere work runs. Fan-out across hundreds of cores still wants remote\nworkers; the point is that the workers and your laptop now agree on what\na compiler is, so both populate one cache."}]}],["$","$L40",null,{"title":"Do I need Docker installed?","id":"do-i-need-docker","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"The README lists \"a functional local container setup\" alongside Nix as a\nprerequisite. Where it is actually exercised in-tree is regenerating the\ntoolchain configurations, which loads a generator image into the local\ncontainer daemon; consuming the checked-in configs is driven by Nix."}]}],["$","$L40",null,{"title":"I'm getting cache misses between local and remote. Where do I look?","id":"cache-misses-local-vs-remote","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Compare the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/nix/store/..."}]," paths in your generated ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lre.bazelrc"}],"\nagainst the ones in the toolchain configs of the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"local-remote-execution"}],"\nmodule at the commit your project pins. A mismatch there is the usual\ncause, and it usually means the flake input and the Bazel module override\nhave drifted apart. They are pinned in two separate files and nothing\nchecks that they agree."]}]}],["$","$L40",null,{"title":"Does one command regenerate all the toolchains?","id":"regenerate-all-toolchains","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["No. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"generate-toolchains"}]," regenerates the Java configuration only; C++ and\nRust have their own separate commands. No single in-tree target runs all\nthree, so a flake update needs all of them."]}]}],["$","$L40",null,{"title":"Is the C++ toolchain fully hermetic?","id":"is-the-cc-toolchain-fully-hermetic","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Not quite, and the source says so. In-tree TODOs in\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"local-remote-execution/overlays/stdenv.nix"}]," record that the result is\nnot a pure Clang/LLVM toolchain, that an unwanted ",["$","code",null,{"children":"libgcc_s"}]," dependency\nremains, and that the stdenv used for the Cargo build and the \"mostly\nhermetic\" LLVM toolchain used by the Bazel build are still two separate\ntoolchains. LRE substantially improves hermeticity; it does not currently\ncomplete it."]}]}]]}]
